{
  "about": "The one case table for the pace spread rule (D134, which replaced D128's numbers). Read by api/tests/PaceSpreadTest.php (App\\\\Services\\\\PaceSpread) and mobile/test/spread_target_test.dart (buildSpreadTarget), so the committee's cover screen and the early nudge agree. Each case gives the viewer's unit and the groups on a run. A group has unit (mi|km), from and to in seconds per that unit (to null for a single pace, from null for a group with no pace), kind (default run) and led (default true; an unled group counts for nothing). Expected: empty (no led group with a pace), gaps as [fast, slow] whole seconds in the viewer's unit (the stretch a new group would fit: 15 s inside each edge of a gap up to a minute, 30 s inside for a bigger one), fasterEnd and slowerEnd (the pace asked for, whole seconds: the fastest group's fast edge less 30 s, or the slowest group's slow edge plus 30 s; null when the end is within 30 s of 8:00 / 12:00) and jogWalk (a led jog/walk group with no pace). Constants per mile: targets 8:00 to 12:00, a gap is more than 30 s, a range gap more than 60 s.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no groups at all",
      "unit": "mi",
      "groups": [],
      "expect": {
        "empty": true,
        "gaps": [],
        "fasterEnd": null,
        "slowerEnd": null,
        "jogWalk": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "only an unled group counts for nothing",
      "unit": "mi",
      "groups": [
        {
          "unit": "mi",
          "from": 540,
          "to": null,
          "led": false
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "empty": true,
        "gaps": [],
        "fasterEnd": null,
        "slowerEnd": null,
        "jogWalk": false
      }
    },
